  5. log-format signature  : container.stdout.log line 1 = {"type":"system","subtype":"init","cwd":"/project",...}   (claude-stream-json — DISTINCT from codex-jsonl)
  6. GIT-READ (verbatim)   : 3b76153a10360cdd30ef1c79d090c329d14fa91a
                             git version 2.34.1
                             3b76153 docs(plan): lane-A discovery plan — mark 'reds have no Bash/never invoke git' SUPERSEDED by P7 executed evidence
  7. BOUNDED-WRITE (verbatim, refused):
                             touch: cannot touch '/project/.red-write-canary': Read-only file system   → touch_exit=1
                             bash: line 1: /project/CANARY: Read-only file system                        → redir_exit=1
                             (canary NOT created; shell exited non-zero because both writes failed — that failure IS the evidence)
                             MOUNT: /run/host_mark/Users on /project type fakeowner (ro,nosuid,nodev,relatime,fakeowner)

── ARM C — pi  [VERIFIED FACT: NOT DISPATCHABLE AS A RED ON THIS HOST — no execution exists] ──
  run / task               : run-p7-diag-pi-51ca9a / task-red-wide-5bf8c0   (status=failed, no container, no manifest)
  forge refusal (verbatim) : "role 'red-wide' requires a tool-capable model (it produces structured result.json
                             output) but the resolved model is not tool-capable (profile 'pi-groq', model
                             'openai/gpt-oss-120b', alias 'review')."
  Root cause               : the ONLY installed Pi profile is `pi-groq` → runtime pi-apikey, model openai/gpt-oss-120b
                             (Groq), which is not tool-capable. Reds require a tool-capable model, so forge FAIL-CLOSES
                             the dispatch before spawning a container. Double-confirmed (tmux launch + synchronous run,
                             both full-PATH). Per campaign scope the policy/runtime was NOT modified to force a pass.
                             ⇒ There is NO genuine Pi red execution. Any claim that "Pi executed Bash/git-read under a
                             red dispatch" or "all three runtimes executed the write-refusal arm" is FALSE / withdrawn.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
SECTION 1b — CORRECTED CONCLUSIONS (what the genuine evidence supports, and at what label)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
C1. [VERIFIED FACT, 2 distinct runtimes] A read-only red EXECUTES Bash and `git rev-parse HEAD` / `git log`.
    Demonstrated under TWO genuinely-distinct, manifest-verified runtimes: codex-subscription (kind=codex) and
    claude-oauth (kind=claude-code) — distinct kind, logFormat, controlPlane path, AND distinct stdout log-line
    signatures. PRD-a §4.2's original "no Bash / do not invoke git" is FALSIFIED.
C2. [VERIFIED FACT] The `:ro` project mount REFUSES every write (touch + redirect both "Read-only file system",
    exit 1; no file created). Demonstrated under BOTH executed runtimes; mount line `fakeowner (ro,...)`.
C3. [INFERENCE — NOT three-runtime execution] Capability-PRESENCE (bash/git/node in the container) is a property
    of the shared agent IMAGE, not of the runtime: the IDENTITY block finds the same `/usr/bin/{bash,git,node}`
    regardless of which CLI orchestrates. So the capability holds for any runtime that CAN dispatch a red; the two
    that ran corroborate it. This is an image-level inference, not a per-runtime execution claim.
C4. [INFERENCE — OS-level, below the runtime] The write-refusal is enforced by forge's spawn mounting /project
    `:ro` on the container (kernel EROFS), INDEPENDENT of the CLI inside. Two genuinely-distinct runtimes hitting
    identical EROFS corroborates that the enforcement is runtime-independent by construction. It is NOT, and must
    not be stated as, "all three runtimes executed the write-refusal arm."
C5. [VERIFIED FACT] Capability-availability (run commands / read git = YES) and filesystem-mutation-authority
    (write = NO) are DISTINCT. PROJECT_MODE=ro governs mutation authority only; it neither grants nor removes
    git-read. FG-559 repairs repository VISIBILITY for linked worktrees; it does not affect tool availability.

